    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="7ae6252e-f7ab-553c-a412-6da54deb8442" activityNameId="f95cedc0-9d71-5f2d-ad20-7f04e1b0b946" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Thomas meal, as P2O5, at regional storehouse</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Thomas meal, as P2O5, at regional storehouse
Values refer to 1 kg P2O5 in thomas meal, resp. 5.88 kg thomas meal with a P2O5-content of 17 weight-%. ;
Synonyms: Thomas-Schlacke, Thomas slag; 
UUID: 6fb9d6e8-b9cf-3820-a5f2-3b9b60e22614
Process energy requirements were taken into account to convert the by-product thomas slag into a commercial  fertiliser. Additionally, transports from the plant to the regional storehouse were supplemented. No data on process emissions were available. Infrastructure and land use were included by means of a proxy-module.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Energy requirements given in the reference were roughly approximated for a commonly used technology for this product.
Time period: Year when reference used for this inventory was published.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data based on a study focussing on the situation in the European Union. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6fb9d6e8-b9cf-3820-a5f2-3b9b60e22614.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
